content='''<div class="m7-hide"><p><a href="#m7-form" class="download">Use the free weekly worksheet</a> · <a href="/downloads/meal-planning-worksheet.pdf" download>Download the two-page blank/example PDF</a></p><p>Plan one seven-day period and enter ingredient needs separately. This manual planner does not read recipes or automatically scale ingredients when servings change.</p><h2 id="m7-start">Enter your plan</h2><form id="m7-form"><label>Plan label (max 100 characters)<input id="m7-name" maxlength="100" required></label><label>First date of this seven-day plan<input id="m7-week" type="date" min="1900-01-01" max="2200-12-25" required></label><h3>Meal slots (1–21)</h3><p>Use each day/Breakfast, Lunch or Dinner slot once. Day 1 is the entered first date, not necessarily Monday. A serving is a planned eating occasion, not a unique person.</p><div id="m7-meals"></div><button id="m7-add-meal" type="button">Add meal</button><h3>Manual ingredient quantities (0–50)</h3><p>Enter the total needed for your chosen recipes and the usable stock in the same unit. Use each ingredient/unit once. No unit conversion or recipe calculation is provided.</p><div id="m7-ingredients"></div><button id="m7-add-ingredient" type="button">Add ingredient</button><p><button type="submit">Review meal plan</button><button id="m7-sample" type="button">Load fictional example</button></p></form><p id="m7-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><h2>Your reviewed meal plan</h2><div id="m7-result" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="m7-hide"><h2>Keep an editable copy</h2><p>No automatic saving. Reloading or closing this page loses entries unless you download a JSON backup. Entries are not sent by this worksheet. CSV and print are static reports; JSON restores editable inputs only in this tool.</p><button id="m7-backup" type="button">Download JSON backup</button><label>Import same-tool JSON (128 KB maximum)<input id="m7-import" type="file" accept="application/json,.json"></label><button id="m7-csv" type="button" disabled>Download reviewed CSV</button><button id="m7-print" type="button" disabled>Print / Save PDF</button><button id="m7-clear" type="button">Clear page entries</button><dialog id="m7-replace-dialog"><p id="m7-replace-label"></p><button id="m7-confirm" type="button">Replace entries</button><button id="m7-cancel" type="button">Cancel replacement</button></dialog><dialog id="m7-clear-dialog"><p>Clear the current page entries? Download a backup first if needed.</p><button id="m7-clear-confirm" type="button">Clear entries</button><button id="m7-clear-cancel" type="button">Keep entries</button></dialog><h2 id="meal-guide">How to use this meal-planning worksheet</h2><p>Choose a plan label and first date. Add up to 21 unique main-meal slots across seven days. Each meal needs a label, 1–24 whole servings and 0–600 whole prep minutes. Missing slots remain unplanned; they are not treated as skipped meals, completed work or a recommendation about eating frequency.</p><p>Check your chosen recipes and preferences separately. Enter 0–50 ingredient lines, each with a name, unit, total quantity needed and usable stock. Supported units are g, kg, mL, L and each. Quantities are nonnegative up to 1,000,000 with at most three decimals. Convert quantities yourself before using them together; the tool does not treat 1 kg as 1 g or combine entries across units.</p><h3>Shopping formula and original fictional example</h3><p>Additional quantity to buy = max(0, total needed − usable stock), calculated for each ingredient/unit. The planner uses thousandths internally to avoid common decimal subtraction artifacts. It does not add unlike ingredient quantities into a misleading grand total.</p><p>The sample starts November 16, 2026 and ends November 22. Three first-day meals each have four servings and prep times of 10, 20 and 30 minutes: 3 of 21 slots planned, 18 unplanned, 12 serving-occasions and 60 summed prep minutes. That does not mean twelve different people or sixty minutes on an automatically scheduled kitchen calendar.</p><p>Rice needed 600 g less 250 g usable stock leaves 350 g to buy. Tomatoes needed 800 g with 900 g stock leave zero to buy. Two entered units of beans less one in stock leave one to buy. Those are three independent manual ingredient lines, not automatically generated recipes or a complete ingredient list for the example meals.</p><h3>Review and save deliberately</h3><p>Review the report before shopping. Every edit clears the old report and disables CSV/print until reviewed again. Loading the sample, importing a validated same-tool backup and clearing the page require confirmation. Import does not merge plans. JSON keeps editable input fields; CSV includes the reviewed meal schedule, ingredient quantities, summary and limitations. Browser printing opens your device's print dialog; inspect pagination.</p><p>The separate two-page US Letter landscape PDF is a static blank/example writing sheet, not fillable and not an editable backup. Without JavaScript, the guide and static PDF remain available. Keep important backups in a place you control.</p><h3>Practical questions</h3><p><strong>Does changing servings scale groceries?</strong> No. Update ingredient quantities from your chosen recipe yourself.</p><p><strong>Can I use two units for the same ingredient?</strong> They stay separate and trigger a review note; no conversion or consolidation occurs. Combine each ingredient/unit's need and stock once to avoid duplicate counting.</p><p><strong>Does this validate a diet, allergens or food handling?</strong> No. It organizes labels and quantities, without nutrition, allergy or food-safety checks, cost estimates, ordering or delivery.</p><p>Use the <a href="/tools/time-blocking-template/">time-blocking worksheet</a> for actual calendar windows and the <a href="/journal/weekly-planner-2026-free-templates/">weekly planner guide</a> for broader commitments. These are separate manual tools; entries do not sync between them.</p></div>'''
page('meal-planning-worksheet','Free Meal Planning Worksheet: Weekly Plan & Shopping List','Plan seven days of meal slots, servings and prep time. Enter ingredient needs and usable stock for a manual shopping list, JSON backup, CSV report and printable PDF.',content,'tools')
p=R/'tools/meal-planning-worksheet/index.html';s=p.read_text();extra='''<style>#m7-form,#m7-start,#meal-guide{scroll-margin-top:110px}.m7-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;padding:18px;margin:16px 0;border:1px solid #bdd0ca;border-radius:10px;min-width:0}.m7-row legend{font-weight:700}.m7-row label{margin:0!important;min-width:0}#m7-form select{width:100%;padding:10px;font:inherit}#m7-form input{min-width:0}#m7-form button{background:#176c66;color:white;border:0;border-radius:6px}#m7-result .table-wrap:focus{outline:3px solid #176c66}#m7-result caption{text-align:left;font-weight:700}dialog{max-width:460px;border:1px solid #bdd0ca;border-radius:12px}.reading p{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:650px){.m7-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}.m7-row button{justify-self:start}}@media print{#m7-result{display:block}.reading{border:0}#m7-result table{min-width:0!important;table-layout:fixed;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:9pt}#m7-result .table-wrap{overflow:visible}#m7-result h3{break-after:avoid}@page{size:landscape;margin:12mm}}</style>''';s=s.replace('</head>',extra+'</head>',1)
# Keep the free-use CTA and controls close to the top; the conceptual cover illustrates the guide.
m=re.search(r'<figure class="article-feature">.*?</figure>',s);fig=m[0];s=s.replace(fig,'',1).replace('<h2 id="meal-guide">',fig+'<h2 id="meal-guide">',1)
p.write_text(s)
